  "researchNotes": "1) Licence: 'sacombank' is on data/licensed-institutions.json. Legal name there is Ngân hàng TMCP Sài Gòn Tài Lộc (formerly Sài Gòn Thương Tín); the bank's T&C and PDFs use the new name. 2) Key finding: Sacombank does NOT publish an offered rate range for its salary loans (online or branch) or its consumer overdraft. Pages say 'Competitive interest rates' and point to a rate tool whose loan tab shows only base rates (effective 26/05/2026: 6,5% to 10,5%/năm by term, basis not stated), recorded as a benchmark on the branch salary loan. A monthly average-lending-rate notice exists (March 2026) but its figure was not readable and it is not a product rate. 3) The only product with published rates is the credit-card-holder loan on SACOMBANK PAY (flat 1,2-1,5%/tháng), but two undated official documents disagree and it needs a Sacombank credit card, so it is excluded from ranking. 4) Fees come from the credit-contract fee schedule effective 09/04/2026 (phi-tin-dung.pdf): online salary loan early repayment free; commitment fee 2% (100k-300k VND) on the online salary loan; late interest 10%/năm; counter loans early repayment from 3% (years 1-2) and 2% (from year 3), min 200.000. 5) Conflicts: online salary loan max 50 triệu (product page) vs 100 triệu (T&C 12/09/2024); card-loan rates FAQ vs rate sheet. 6) Gaps: no Vietnamese product page found (guessed URLs 404, English pages used); age, income and document rules for the online salary loan; insurance cost for the branch loan; overdraft rate, fee and term. 7) Surprising: the 2% commitment fee on the online salary loan is not on the product page; the branch loan lets the borrower pick flat or reducing repayment. Time-limited promo packages (from 7,5%/năm, 40.000 tỷ) were not recorded.",
  "retrievedAt": "2026-11-02"
